.TH MINTTOYS 1 2026-10-09 "MintToys" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minttoys \- power-user utilities for Linux Mint Cinnamon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minttoys awake on
.RB [ \-\-for
.I DURATION
|
.B \-\-until
.IR HH:MM ]
.RB [ \-\-screen " | " \-\-no\-screen ]
.br
.B minttoys awake
.RB { off | toggle | status }
.br
.B minttoys lightswitch
.RB [ status " | " toggle ]
.br
.B minttoys modules
.RB [ list " | " enable
.I MODULE
|
.B disable
.IR MODULE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minttoys
controls MintToys from a terminal or a script. It talks to the MintToys service of the
current session, which starts on its own if it is not running yet.
.SS Awake
Awake keeps the computer from going to sleep, without changing the power settings. Every
.B awake
command prints the state it leaves Awake in.
.TP
.B on
Keeps the computer awake until it is turned off, or for a time, or until a time of day.
.TP
.B off
Lets the computer sleep again as the power settings say.
.TP
.B toggle
Turns Awake off when it is on, and on as set in MintToys when it is off. This is the
command to put on a keyboard shortcut.
.TP
.B status
Prints whether Awake is on, and for how long.
.SS Light Switch
Light Switch switches the desktop between Linux Mint's dark mode and its day mode (Mixed
or Light), the way the Themes window does, by Night Light's schedule or at set times. Both
commands print the mode the desktop is in, today's dark hours and its keyboard shortcut.
.PP
When it comes on, Light Switch adds a custom keyboard shortcut to Cinnamon,
.BR Super+Ctrl+Shift+D ,
named
.BR "MintToys: Light Switch" ,
unless those keys are in use already. Its keys can be changed in the Keyboard settings.
It is taken away when Light Switch, or its shortcut, is switched off in MintToys.
.TP
.B status
Prints the mode and the dark hours, and why Light Switch cannot switch the desktop if it
cannot. The default.
.TP
.B toggle
Switches to dark now, or back to the day's mode, until the schedule next changes. This is
the command to put on a keyboard shortcut.
.SS Modules
.TP
.B list
Lists the modules, and whether each is on, off, or failed and why. The default.
.TP
.BI enable " MODULE"
Switches a module on, and keeps it on at the next login.
.TP
.BI disable " MODULE"
Switches a module off, and keeps it off.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-for " DURATION"
Stays awake this long: minutes (\fB90\fR or \fB90m\fR), hours (\fB2h\fR), or both
(\fB1h30m\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-until " HH:MM"
Stays awake until this time of day; a time already past today means tomorrow.
.TP
.BR \-\-screen ", " \-\-no\-screen
Keeps the screen on as well, or lets it turn off while the computer stays awake. Without
either, the setting from the panel icon applies.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 1
MintToys could not do it: it is not running, the module is switched off, or it refused
the request. The reason is printed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is wrong.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/minttoys/config.json
The settings, one section per module.
.SH NOTES
Removing the package cannot reach into a user's own settings: a keyboard shortcut a tool
added stays in Cinnamon's custom shortcuts until the tool is switched off first, or the
shortcut is removed in the Keyboard settings.
.SH EXAMPLES
Stay awake for an hour and a half, with the screen on:
.PP
.RS
minttoys awake on \-\-for 1h30m \-\-screen
.RE
.PP
Stay awake until six in the evening:
.PP
.RS
minttoys awake on \-\-until 18:00
.RE
.PP
Switch Light Switch on, then go dark now:
.PP
.RS
minttoys modules enable lightswitch
.br
minttoys lightswitch toggle
.RE
